    <us-gaap:RevenueRecognitionPolicyTextBlock contextRef="c-1" id="f-397">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;We disaggregate our revenues by segment (Note 6), by products and services (as presented on our condensed consolidated statements of operations), and for our QCT (Qualcomm CDMA Technologies) segment, by revenue stream, which is based on the industry and application in which our products are sold (as presented below). In certain cases, the determination of QCT revenues by industry and application requires the use of certain assumptions. Substantially all of QCT&#x2019;s revenues consist of equipment revenues that are recognized at a point in time, and substantially all of QTL&#x2019;s (Qualcomm Technology Licensing) revenues represent licensing revenues that are recognized over time and are principally from royalties generated through our licensees&#x2019; sales of mobile handsets.&lt;/span&gt;</us-gaap:RevenueRecognitionPolicyTextBlock>
